From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:59:55 +0000
Subject: src: stop including trace_event.h from node_internals.h

node_internals.h does not use anything from tracing/trace_event.h. The
include is a leftover umbrella include from when it was moved out of
node.h (https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/10959), and it drags the
tracing headers (and, with V8_USE_PERFETTO, the Perfetto SDK headers)
into every translation unit that includes node_internals.h.

Drop it and include tracing/trace_event.h directly in the files that
use the TRACE_* macros. The TRACING_CATEGORY_NODE* and
NODE_TRACE_CATEGORY_ENABLED macros stay in node_internals.h; they only
need trace_event.h at their expansion sites, which now include it.
node_test_fixture.h relied on the include for tracing::Agent, so it
now includes tracing/agent.h.

This should be upstreamed.

